  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper introduces a quantum Chebyshev transform and orthonormal Chebyshev feature map for quantum machine learning. Demonstrations include learning a lognormal Black–Scholes asset-price distribution using a 5‑qubit embedding with a depth‑14 variational ansatz trained for 5,000 epochs and sampling with 10^6 shots, and a small 2‑qubit toy experiment learning a linear distribution and sampling it on an extended 8‑qubit register. All results are obtained via noiseless simulation in the Yao.jl framework.",
